fix(state): the PO's plain terminal discard-feature takes the direct route in a catalogue project

The Critic course admission and the discard writer both name discard-feature,
run in the PO's own terminal, as the recovery for a damaged Critic course.
In a project that has a session-authority catalogue the route demanded an
owning lifecycle context that a plain shell never has, so it refused with
SDC-AUTHORITY-UNAVAILABLE (companion-owning-lifecycle-context-required),
wrote nothing, and the recovery it prescribed could not run (live Codex
greenfield, 2026-11-16).

discard-feature joins the verbs that take the direct PF-54 route when no
owning context exists, like the design verbs and close-feature with a
coordinator binding: refused while a State operation is in flight, and the
writer still proves --by, --reason, the active feature, the
structurally-unsatisfiable-close condition and the cleanup-binding release.
The po-only-discard-boundary hook still keeps the agent from running it.

A case in the result-bootstrap suite pins both: the discard runs in a
catalogue project and leaves no binding behind, and it is held while a State
operation is in flight.

